# VideoBrief — Supabase + Drizzle

## Roles

| Concern | Tool |
|---------|------|
| Auth / session cookies | `@supabase/ssr` |
| App queries / mutations | Drizzle + Postgres |
| Schema + migrations | Drizzle Kit |
| Authorization boundary | Postgres RLS (+ app checks) |

## Schema habits

- UUID PKs with defaults where appropriate
- `createdAt` / `updatedAt` on tables
- Export inferred types (`$inferSelect` / `$inferInsert`)
- Hybrid model: shared video/transcript by YouTube id; per-user analysis & context
- Indexes on foreign keys and frequent filters (`userId`, `youtubeId`, analysis status)

## Migrations

1. Edit `src/db/schema.ts`
2. `pnpm drizzle-kit generate`
3. `pnpm drizzle-kit migrate`
4. Ship **RLS policies in the same change** as new user-owned tables

Never disable RLS to “make dev easier.” Never trust browser `user_id`.

## Auth

- Email/password + Google OAuth
- Soft email confirmation — allow use before verify; nudge later
- Middleware / server layouts protect private routes
- Server: `createServerClient` with full cookie `getAll`/`setAll` where writes happen

## Database URL

Use the **Transaction pooler** URI from Dashboard → **Connect**:
`aws-*-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543`, user `postgres.<project_ref>`.

Direct `db.<ref>.supabase.co:5432` is often **IPv6-only** (`ENETUNREACH` locally).

## Authz / onboarding

- Middleware: session refresh + unauthenticated redirects only
- App gates (onboarding, etc.): RSC / Server Actions via **Drizzle**, not PostgREST
- Source of truth: `profiles.onboarding_completed` (no client cookie flags)

## Clients

- Browser: anon key only
- Server user-scoped: SSR client
- Service role: rare, server-only, comment why when used (e.g. shared transcript upsert)

Use Supabase MCP (read-only preferred) for live schema/RLS inspection when configured.
